ery seem to be unnecessary or redundant. Subqueries could be used to simplify the logic and reduce the number of joins.\n3. Use aggregations consistently: The query uses both SUM and COUNT aggregations. It would be better to use a consistent aggregation function throughout the query, such as SUM for all calculations.\n4. Simplify the logical project: The LogicalProject operator is used extensively in the query. This could be simplified by using more concise syntax or by breaking it down into smaller, more manageable pieces.\n\nHere's an example of how the rewritten query might look:\n```sql\nSELECT \n  channel,\n  SUM(sales) AS total_sales,\n  COUNT(*) AS number_of_sales\nFROM (\n  SELECT \n    'web' AS channel,\n    ws_item_sk,\n    ws_sold_date_sk,\n    ws_wholesale_cost,\n    d_week_seq\n  FROM web_sales\n  WHERE \n    ws_sold_date_sk >= DATE '1998-01-01'\n    AND ws_sold_date_sk <= DATE '1999-12-31'\n    AND ws_wholesale_cost >= 73\n    AND ws_wholesale_cost <= 93\n  UNION ALL\n  SELECT \n    'catalog' AS channel,\n    cs_item_sk,\n    cs_sold_date_sk,\n    cs_wholesale_cost,\n    d_week_seq\n  FROM catalog_sales\n  WHERE \n    cs_sold_date_sk >= DATE '1998-01-01'\n    AND cs_sold_date_sk <= DATE '1999-12-31'\n    AND cs_wholesale_cost >= 73\n    AND cs_wholesale_cost <= 93\n  UNION ALL\n  SELECT \n    'store' AS channel,\n    ss_item_sk,\n    ss_sold_date_sk,\n    ss_wholesale_cost,\n    d_week_seq\n  FROM store_sales\n  WHERE \n    ss_sold_date_sk >= DATE '1998-01-01'\n    AND ss_sold_date_sk <= DATE '1999-12-31'\n    AND ss_wholesale_cost >= 73\n    AND ss_wholesale_cost <= 93\n) AS subquery\nJOIN date_dim ON d_week_seq = subquery.d_week_seq\nGROUP BY channel;\n```\nThis rewritten query uses subqueries to simplify the logic and reduce the number of joins. It also uses a consistent aggregation function (SUM) throughout the query. The LogicalProject operator is simplified by using more concise syntax.\n\nPlease note that this is just an example, and you may nee